    choices: ["Cotton planting on land taken from Native nations", "A legal revival of the Atlantic slave trade", "Planters' shift from cotton to wheat and corn", "A federal ban on slavery in the Gulf states"],
    why: ["Correct. With the cotton gin and the removal of the Creek, Choctaw, and Chickasaw, planters moved into the Deep South and brought or bought enslaved workers to grow cotton.", "The Atlantic trade was banned in 1808 and was never made legal again.", "The Deep South's planters grew more cotton, not less.", "No such ban existed; both states allowed slavery."],
